{"requirements":[{"id":"ssh-group-restriction","requirement":"On node1, SSH login access is restricted to members of the local remote-access group while SSH remains operational.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The effective and final daemon policy is `AllowGroups remote-access`, sshd is syntax-valid, active, enabled, and listening. An authenticated remote-access member successfully logged in, while a valid temporary nonmember was rejected explicitly because its groups were not listed in AllowGroups. The same behavior and policy were observed after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-330ae352eae845d1","cmd-dfe8acc6287f4b9d","cmd-5d451ec44d6f4109","cmd-291f3a51e5cc4987","cmd-d53368da00ed4dc0","cmd-b3c61ffc69d74934"]},{"id":"opsadmin-membership","requirement":"The local remote-access group exists and opsadmin belongs to it.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The baseline lacked both objects. The executor created the local group and account, added opsadmin, and final `id` and `getent group` output confirm persistent membership after reboot and cleanup.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a89130af66934255","cmd-b1caf400da384262","cmd-291f3a51e5cc4987","cmd-b3c61ffc69d74934"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"Chronological review found no unnecessary mutations. Account/group creation and the validated sshd drop-in directly implemented the contract. Temporary passwords, keys, probe accounts, and marker files were bounded prerequisites for meaningful allow/deny and restart tests; the probes and credentials were removed, marker files deleted, and opsadmin's temporary password locked. The transient reboot unit served the mandatory restart protocol and disappeared with reboot. Final observations show no failed services, no added socket exposure, and healthy package state; temporary-file differences are normal per-boot systemd directories.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b1caf400da384262","cmd-9b3049a106a540df","cmd-dfe8acc6287f4b9d","cmd-440cb74b26d54042","cmd-328b3d04a4054471","cmd-d53368da00ed4dc0","cmd-b3c61ffc69d74934","global:before_prepare:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:before_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"Both material task outcomes are satisfied with direct final-state and behavioral evidence. The independent node-restart protocol is also complete: it captures a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, a changed boot identity, recovered sshd and persistent account/configuration state, and successful member plus rejected nonmember behavior after reboot. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":[]}
